WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.560
You're going to Okinawa next week.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.770
What's hard is forever.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.440
To be famous forever, you need a legend.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.070
I can't find the demo tape
 for our debut song!

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:12.090
We have to sing the same one.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.990
If we're not careful, we may not 
be able to sing it after tomorrow.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.780
<i>Making the dream! (Yeah!)</i>

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:40.810
<b>Entertainment News TIME!</b>

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:40.810
<b>IDOLiSH7 Concerts Flourishing!</b>

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.530
<i>Making the sky! (Flight!)</i>

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:22.180
Yesterday a new whirlwind idol group was born.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:22.180
<i>Past all others</i>

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:25.580
<i>Step! (Yes!) Step! (Yes!) we'll advance</i>

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.390
Their name is IDOLiSH7.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.300
I've heard of these boys.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.300
<i>The future is in our hands</i>

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.040
They're finally debuting, huh?

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.300
That's so exciting!

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.000
<i>Shaking your heart (Say!)</i>

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.050
Members Osaka Sogo-san and Yotsuba Tamaki-san

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.860
<i>Shaking your beat (Shout!)</i>

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.050
also work as a separate unit called MEZZO".

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.370
<i>I will deliver</i>

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.940
And their leader Nikaido Yamato-san 
also works as an actor.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.370
<i>Jump! (High!) Jump! (High!)</i>

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.210
<i>This vivid GENERATiON with you</i>

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.810
What a talented group.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:42.650
Good evening.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:43.810
We're IDOLiSH7!

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.400
We were able to debut thanks to all our fans.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.970
I feel so much better when 
it's all seven of us.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.040
We were anxious when MEZZO" debuted first,

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.240
but thanks to them, we got
 our names out there.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:00:59.740
How do you feel, Sogo-san?

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:00.580
Huh?

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.980
About debuting thanks to MEZZO".

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:04.950
Oh, right. We didn't do anything.

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.090
It's because the rest of 
you kept working so hard.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:09.230
Thank you.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.990
We'd like to move on to 
the press conference now.

00:01:11.990 --> 00:01:14.840
Please raise your hand 
if you have a question.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.300
Yes, we'll start with you.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.980
I'm with <i>BNO Magazine</i>.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.810
Is there a story behind your 
debut song "MONSTER GENERATiON"

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.060
or anything you'd like to say about it?

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:28.480
Oh, yeah. Our debut song is, uh...

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:32.710
It's a really important song to us.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:34.030
Right, Riku?

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.610
Uh, yeah!

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:39.200
"MONSTER GENERATiON" is the 
first song we sang onstage.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.170
And the calls during the song are fun, right?

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.350
Our album tour is starting soon.

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:46.850
We hope you'll enjoy it 
at our concerts with us.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:59.180
Gazing at the distant sky...

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:02.720
Someday we'll make it past there

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.310
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.150
We don't know what's right

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.380
So we Try and Jump!

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.530
Slamming face first into 
challenges and laughing

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:25.160
For us It's Only Way!

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.320
Make it shake (For Your Sky)

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.820
Make it reach (For Your Heart)

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.340
We'll change any and all kinds of pain

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:35.500
Do Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.340
Live! (Yeah!)

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.760
In the light!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.550
(One, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven Go!)

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:47.020
Yes Glory Days! Together 
we'll run through them

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.810
If your voice (Fuu!) reverberates (Dream!)

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:53.330
Then your wishes will become 
destiny (Singing New World!)

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:59.820
Give rise now to Age of Stage!

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:06.790
The future surely lies on the other side

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:09.710
Yes... It will keep on evolving

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:13.080
Our WiSH VOYAGE

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:19.340
Build a rainbow Next Harmony!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:29.060
I told you they'd ask about our debut song.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:30.510
You practiced so much.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.700
Sorry.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.230
I understand how you feel, but...

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:37.480
It's hard to change gears so quickly.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.870
I'm really sorry.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:45.410
We even filmed a PV, but 
we can't use the song.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.370
It's not your fault.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.040
It's TRIGGER's fault.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:49.540
Tamaki-kun!

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.290
Isn't it?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.860
Their new song was a total ripoff of ours.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.690
Maybe they stole it.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.510
Why aren't we suing them?

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:02.600
Not only do we not have proof, 
but they could sue us for libel.

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:05.340
I'd like to avoid jinxing our debut.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.180
I'd like to think the members of 
TRIGGER itself weren't involved.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.660
I'm very disappointed.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:16.690
I wanted you all to sing it.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.610
You wanted us to sing it?

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.510
I won't forgive them.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.410
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:30.700
I don't know who did it, but 
they'll regret angering me.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.130
What's with you?

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.830
Just say "oh" like you always do.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.290
Excuse me.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:38.750
This is Takanashi.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.260
What?! Really?

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.950
Yes, thank you!

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.140
Goodbye.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:50.970
IDOLiSH7 has gotten a regular show!

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.220
It's even named after us!

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:53.390
What?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:59.550
Manager, is that good news or bad news?

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.630
It's super good news!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.330
We're getting our own show!

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:04.350
Really?

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.370
You should be happier.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.660
Wow! All right!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.800
Tama, you're so honest.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.140
An album tour and a namesake show.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:14.290
We'll be getting busier.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.750
Bring it on!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.710
We can't worry about this forever.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.460
Let's smile and work hard 
for the sake of our fans.

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:22.460
Yeah!

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.650
Come on, Nagi. Put that scowl away.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.450
You're ruining your handsome face.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.970
And your face is 80 percent of your appeal.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.210
Oh...

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.780
Mitsuki, are you after my body?

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.600
Why would I want the other 20 percent?!

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.350
This is our moment of truth.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.770
Let's focus on making the 
album tour a success first.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.020
Yeah!

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.020
Yes!

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:45.170
We're in Osaka!

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:47.030
Mitsu, you always shout first.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:53.170
I want takoyaki, okonomiyaki, 
fried skewers, and offal!

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:54.230
Let's eat all of them.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.830
We can't eat all that—

00:05:58.850 --> 00:05:59.910
What's wrong, Iori?

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.300
You want the local mascot?

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:06.050
I'm not at all interested 
in something so cheap.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.460
<b>Taiko no Tatsujin</b>

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.420
<b>Osaka Specialties          Takoyaki | Okonomiyaki</b>

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.320
It's so good.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:28.320
Hot, hot!

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.450
Iori, one bite.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:32.450
Huh?

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.290
Ah...

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.230
Nii-san.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:36.540
I'll give you some of mine.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:37.870
You're hopeless.

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:40.750
Hot!

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.010
Iori!

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:43.210
Sorry!

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.900
Oh, it's a two-man act.

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.340
MEZZO" is meeting us once 
they're done working, right?

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.080
I hope we have time to eat together.

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:52.970
Yes.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:57.060
Once our tour is finished, 
our regular show starts.

00:06:57.530 --> 00:07:02.530
I wish we could assign them a manager, 
but Banri-san and the others are too busy.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.190
If only I could be in two places at once.

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:08.070
Manager, don't push yourself.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.470
Let's buy souvenirs for them.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:12.950
They won't have time to go sightseeing.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.630
Oh, good idea.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:17.410
Let's buy them matching straps.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.730
No way.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.240
They're not that close.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.080
Even though they sing together?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.420
Surely they're getting along by now.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:30.990
Why didn't you wake me?

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.750
I fell asleep, too.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:33.720
Let's grab a taxi.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.980
It'll be faster if we run.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:37.940
Tamaki-kun, wait!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.730
When does rehearsal start?

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:49.430
Are you okay?

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:50.740
Want me to carry your stuff?

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.240
Why?

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.180
I have more stamina.

00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:58.080
And you haven't been looking well lately.

00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:02.580
I'm fine. It's okay.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.750
Listen, I'm an idiot.

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.550
You have to tell me what you're thinking!

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:13.630
You gotta <i>tell me </i>if you don't like something, 
or you're mad, or you're struggling!

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:16.610
Okay.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.430
Whoa, what an expensive looking car.

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:25.170
It was so shiny.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:26.090
Did you see that?

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.930
So-chan, you okay?

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.220
Want me to carry you?

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.530
Dad...

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:43.700
Okay, good.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.170
Watch out for the sections 
we revised during the show.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.260
Okay.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.290
Thank you.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.520
That was great.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.010
Fantastic!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:54.220
Rikkun, Iorin!

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:56.090
Those names...

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.720
Sorry we're late!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:08:59.580
Tamaki, Sogo-san.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:00.600
Hello.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.430
You guys are on next.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:03.460
Okay.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.280
Don't hurt yourselves.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.400
But go all out.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:14.360
Let's have fun!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.280
Yes!

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:16.200
Yeah.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.030
Let's do a great job and 
hand it off to the next guys!

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.830
Let's go.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.030
Yeah!

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:27.540
Yes, Dancing BEAT!! Even farther away

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:30.880
Night and day!! I want to deliver

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:37.540
Never knowing what it means to 
stand still keep charging ahead

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.890
Right? Dancing BEAT!! An even more wonderful

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:42.140
Night and day!!

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.040
You feel it

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:49.180
Let's abandon our naive feelings somewhere!

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.600
<b>Let's Run Away
 Together</b>

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.980
(Goodbye weak point)

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.660
In such a harsh world they'd only be crushed

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:56.030
To the west, to the east Pythagoras

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:59.910
A delivery with a zany smile

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:03.330
To your city Pythagoras

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.050
[Official] IDOLiSH7
 We're eating okonomiyaki together!
Riku-kun wrote on his with mayonnaise!

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:03.510
[Official] IDOLiSH7
 The concert was so exciting!
 Thank you all for coming!

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:08.170
I wish I could embrace you right now

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:05.500
Sapporo 
Station

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:13.500
And run away with you

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.650
But I can't so my small love

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:23.210
Will never reach you

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:28.180
Thank you!

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.930
Thank you!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.780
Thank you so much!

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.620
Whoop.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.140
Rikkun, what's up?

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:46.970
Huh? Oh.

00:10:46.970 --> 00:10:48.730
We've been to a bunch of places,

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:52.040
but it's always amazing that 
there's people waiting for us.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:54.060
Yeah. It is amazing.

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:57.510
Tamaki, Sogo's been looking for you.

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:59.190
Oh, crap.

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:00.270
Later.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.500
Be careful.

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.350
Yep!

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.310
Are they okay?

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:10.140
Tama's fine, but managing him has 
probably pushed So to his limit.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.230
You think so?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.400
He seems like he'd manage 
everything easily like Iori does.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:18.660
Ichi is brazen. So isn't like him at all.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.910
I know what you mean.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.410
Hey. You guys.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.290
He probably lets his stress build up.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:26.870
Sogo-san.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.530
I'll go with you.

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.520
Huh?

00:11:29.520 --> 00:11:32.070
I'm sorry for making you 
do everything until now.

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:35.850
I've talked to the others, and from 
now on, I plan to focus on MEZZO".

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:39.320
Oh, thanks. But it's their first tour,

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.330
so you should stay with them.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.830
We'll be fine.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:43.300
But—

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.750
It's fine. I prefer being busy.

00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.430
I don't have to think.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:50.430
Sogo-san?

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.230
It's nothing.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:55.360
Tell the others I appreciate 
them worrying about us.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.090
Got it.

00:11:57.090 --> 00:11:59.180
Let me know if you're ever struggling.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:01.100
Thanks. See you later.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.180
Aren't you tired?

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.540
I'm fine. You can sleep.

00:12:13.930 --> 00:12:15.570
I told you.

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:19.410
I'm stupid, so you have to 
tell me what you're feeling.

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:20.900
Tell you what?

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:22.290
What? I—

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:25.300
I'm fine. I'll sleep later.

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:28.010
Oh, really?

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.540
Tamaki-kun, you haven't filled 
out your survey again.

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.130
Sorry, can you wake up?

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.180
Come on. Fill it out.

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:39.250
So-chan, you fill it out.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:45.660
Next Stop: Gunya 
Doors open on this side

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:42.130
I'll read the questions 
to you, so you answer.

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:43.830
Why did you want to become an idol?

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:45.660
To find Aya.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.620
Is it okay if I write that?

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:49.470
Yeah.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:50.660
Okay.

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:53.620
How about you?

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:55.030
I already filled mine out.

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:56.940
What's your real answer?

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.420
Not the one your fans will like.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.420
Osaka Sogo
 Please fill out the questionnaire 
by responding to the questions below.
 Thank you very much for your participation.

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:04.580
It doesn't have to be your hopes and dreams 
or any of that stuff. Just tell me.

00:13:04.580 --> 00:13:06.300
Why are you doing this job?

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.550
Self-proof, I guess.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.220
What's that mean?

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:14.810
Showing the world who you are.

